cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "msa-ad: Measurement System Analysis for Automated-Driving Validation"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of Measurement System Analysis (MSA) methods applied to
  automated-driving validation benches. Provides crossed ANOVA gage repeatability
  and reproducibility (Gage R&R) for continuous safety-margin metrics, bias and
  linearity studies against reference values, attribute agreement analysis with
  Cohen's and Fleiss' kappa for binary pass/fail verdicts, and seeded-fault
  coverage-claim verification with Wilson confidence intervals. Targets
  simulation, hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) and fault-injection test benches.
  Depends only on numpy, scipy and pandas.
type: software
